# SP1 circuit conventions

## Shared I/O (`zk-circuit/io`)

- `zk-circuit-io`: `PrivateInputs`, `PublicOutputs`, Poseidon Merkle helpers
- No `sp1-zkvm` in this crate (guest and native host both depend on it)
- Do not duplicate I/O structs in guest or host
- Poseidon/Merkle/nullifier changes need `zk-circuit-io` `--lib` tests (see `05-tests-security.mdc`)

## Guest (`zk-circuit/guest`)

- Stack-only hot path: fixed arrays (`[u8; 32]`, path depth fixed e.g. 20) — no `Vec` / heap in constraints
- Private inputs stay in guest; public journal = amounts, mint/asset id, nullifier, merkle root
- Commit journal via `sp1_zkvm::io::commit` only after constraints pass
- Guest profile: aggressive opts (`opt-level = 3`, LTO) when wired

## Host (`zk-circuit/host`)

- Drive `sp1_sdk::ProverClient`; fixtures must match guest path/hash scheme
- Serialize Groth16 proof + public values for Anchor ix data; keep packing helpers tested
- Negative tests: non-member leaf must fail closed

## Do not

- Do not change journal field order/layout without updating on-chain parse + vkey
- Do not log secrets (spending keys, full Merkle paths with private leaf) in host output committed to git
